  "freight_commentary": {
    "Dry Bulk Freight": "Capesize: The Capesize C5TC average improved by USD 0.1k/day closing the week at USD 48,954/ day. Trip from Continent to F.East is up by 4.2k/ day at USD 91,494/day, Transatlantic R/V is higher by 8.2k/day at USD 62,938/day, and Bolivar to Rotterdam is higher by 7.8k/day at USD 69,006/ day, while Transpacific R/V is reduced by 4.5k/day at USD 45,863/day. Trip from Tubarao to Rotter- dam is increased by 1.8k/day at USD 45,918/day, China-Brazil R/V is lower by 0.7k/day at USD 50,694/day, and & trip from Saldanha Bay to Qinqdao is increased by 1.8k/day at USD 45,918/ day.\n\nKamsarmax/Panamax: The Kamsarmax P5TC Timecharter average started the week at USD 20,262/day closing with an increase at USD 21,662/day. Trip from Skaw-Gib to F.East is im- proved by 1.3k/day at USD 30,893/day, Pacific R/ Vis up at USD 21,363/day, while Transatlantic R/V is increased by 2.8k/day at USD 21,645/day, and Singapore R/V via Atlantic is increased by 1k/day at USD 21,675/day.\n\nUltramax/Supramax: The Ultramax S11TC average closed the week about USD 0.2k/day higher than its opening at USD 22,579/day. The Supramax S10TC average closed the week about 0.2k/day higher than its opening at USD 20,545/day. The Baltic Su- pramax Asia S3TC average closed the week about 0.3k/day higher than previous week at USD 21,054/ day. N.China one Australian or Pacific R/V is im- proved by 0.2k/day at USD 21,144/day, USG to Skaw Passero is softer by 0.1k/day at USD 32,644/ day. S.China trip via Indonesia to EC India is up by 0.2k/day at USD 25,429/day, trip from S.China via Indonesia to S.China pays USD 16,550/day, while Med/B.Sea to China/S.Korea is increased by 0.7k/ day at USD 26,322/day.\n\nHandysize: The Handysize HS7TC average closed the week improved by 0.4k/day at USD 18,190/day. Skaw-Passero trip to Boston-Galveston pays 1.3k/ day more at USD 14,014/day, Brazil to Cont. pays 0.5k/day more at USD 25,678/day, S.E. Asia trip to Spore/Japan 0.2k/day is softer at USD 17,894/day, China/S.Korea/Japan round trip is reduced at USD 17,244/day, and trip from U.S. Gulf to Cont. is in- creased by 0.9k/day at USD 24,914/day, while N.China-S.Korea-Japan trip to S.E.Asia is increased at USD 18,050/day.",
    "Tanker Freight": "VLCC: average T/CE ended the week down by 8.8k/day at USD 714,143/day. Middle East Gulf to China trip is down by 6.4k/day at USD 1,234,685/ day. West Africa to China trip is down by 20.8k/ day at USD 506,643/day and US Gulf to China trip is down by 0.8k/day at USD 401,101/day.\n\nSuezmax: average T/CE closed the week softer by 4.3k/day at USD 299,424/day. West Africa to Con- tinent trip is down by 8.1k/day at USD 230,625/ day, Black Sea to Mediterranean is down by 0.4k/ day at USD 368,223/day, and Middle East Gulf to Med trip is reduced by 10.1k/day at USD 547,549/ day, while trip from Guyana to ARA is reduced by 19.2k/day at USD 229,180/day.\n\nAframax: average T/CE closed the week higher by 72.1k/day at USD 234,370/day. North Sea to Con- tinent trip is up by 125.1k/day at USD 314,796/ day, Kuwait to Singapore is up by 41.5k/day at USD 264,575/day, while route from Caribbean to US Gulf trip is up by 63.8k/day at USD 186,721/ day. Trip from South East Asia to East Coast Aus- tralia is up by 24k/day at USD 114,905/day & Cross Mediterranean tripis up by 75.1k/day at USD 288,783/day. US Gulf to UK-Continent is improved by 90.5k/day at USD 213,992/day and the East Coast Mexico to US Gulf trip is up by USD 76.6k/ day at USD 209,169/day.\n\nProducts: The LR2 route (TC1) Middle East to Ja- pan is this week higher by 16.7k/day at USD 254,158/day. Trip from (TC15) Med to Far East has increased by 8.1k/day at USD 61,553/day and (TC20) AG to UK Continent is up by 10.4k/day at USD 257,378/day. The LR1 route (TC5) from Mid- dle East Gulf to Japan is up by 15.8k/day at USD 187,550/day, while the (TC8) Middle East Gulf to UK-Continent is up by 10.4k/day at USD 257,378/ day. The MR Atlantic Basket is increased by 10.8k/ day at USD 39,287/day & the MR Pacific Basket earnings are improved by 9.4k/day at USD 70,623/ day. The MR route from Rotterdam to New York (TC2) is firmer by 16.7k/day at USD 254,158/day, (TC6) Intermed (Algeria to Euro Med) earnings are firmer by15.8k/day at USD 187,550/day, (TC14) US Gulf to Continent is up by 6.4k/day at USD 44,331/ day, (TC18) US Gulf to Brazil earnings are higher by 20.5k/day at USD 112,326/day, (TC23) Amsterdam to Le Havre is higher by 7.2k/day at USD 56,549/ day while Yeosu to Botany Bay (TC22) is firmer by 11.2k/day at USD 30,282/day and ARA to West Africa (TC19) is up by 8.2k/day at USD 37,041/day."
