  "dry_snp_activity": "On the Kamsarmax sector, German buyers acquired the “GCL Hazira” - 82K/2021 NACKS for USD 39 mills basis surveys passed, while the sister vessel “New Wavelet” - 82K/2021 NACKS changed hands for USD 38.4 mills ba- sis delivery Q1 2027 and the “Babitonga” - 82K/2019 Tsuneishi changed hands for USD 38.5 mills.\n\nOn the Panamax sector, Chinese buyers acquired the “Good Hope Max” - 77K/2005 Sasebo for USD 12.5 mills. Moving down the sizes, on the Supramax sector, the “YC Aequor” - 57K/2012 Ningbo was sold for high USD 13 mills. Finally, on the Handysize sector, the “CS Calla” - 37K/2011 Tianjin Xingang found new owners for USD 11 mills basis surveys due.",
  "wet_snp_activity": "The tanker S&P market saw significant activity this week, particularly in the VLCC sector. Clients of ADNOC acquired the “Seaking” - 319K/2013 Hyundai Heavy for USD 177 mills, while the “Olympic Target” - 320K/2011 Hyundai Heavy and the “Olympic Light” - 317K/2011 Hyundai Samho were sold enbloc for USD 300 mills. On the same sector, the “Atherina” - 319K/2011 Hyundai Heavy changed hands for USD 146 mills. On the Su- ezmax sector, the “Stella” - 165K/2011 Hyundai Samho was sold for USD 83 mills, while Turkish buyers acquired the Aframax “TP Affinity” - 114K/2016 Hyundai Samho for USD 73 mills. The “Eurointegrity” - 105K/2009 Hyundai Heavy was sold for USD 60 mills. On the Pana- max/LR1 sector, the “London Star” - 74K/2006 New Century changed hands for USD 21.5 mills basis SS/DD due. On the MRs, the scrubber fitted “Puffin Pacific” - 50K/2020 STX was sold for USD 49 mills, while the “Virgen Del Cisne” - 50K/2009 SPP for USD 25.5 mills. The “Atlantic Crown” - 47K/2007 Hyundai Mipo and the “Ocean Sunrise” - 49K/2006 Iwagi Zosen were sold for USD 19.1 mills and USD 17.5 mills, respectively. Finally, the “Vitality” - 37K/2002 Hyundai Mipo and the “Sunflyte” - 37K/2001 Hyundai Mipo were sold enbloc for USD 17 mills.",
